    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Exploring Python Collections: Lists and Strings Essential Guide"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MP1Tan_DYuWK"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Before we get deeper into Python essentials for interview prep, we'll remind ourselves about some Python features - specifically, Python collections — Lists, and Strings. These collections allow Python to group multiple elements, such as numbers or characters, under a single entity.\n",
        "\n",
        "Some of these concepts might already be familiar to you, so you can breeze through the beginning until we get to the meat of the course and the path."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "W4svDeD7Y-4p"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Understanding Python's Collections"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Cj60nkYqZCQK"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "As our starting point, it's crucial to understand what Python collections are. They help us manage multiple values efficiently and are categorized into Lists, Tuples, Sets, and Dictionaries.\n",
        "\n",
        "We will focus mainly on Lists and Strings. A fun fact here is that Lists are mutable (we can change them after creation), while strings are immutable (unalterable post-creation). Let's see examples:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "v2awABvcZNlK"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Defining a list and a string\n",
        "my_list = [1, 2, 3, 4]\n",
        "my_string = \"hello\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Now let's try to change the first element of both these collections\n",
        "my_list[0] = 100\n",
        "# The below line will throw an error\n",
        "my_string[0] = 'H'"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 176
        },
        "id": "bXia3IwVZeRZ",
        "outputId": "ed998684-eae6-4054-cb7d-90f48b7ed1c9"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
