      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Looping in Python: Understanding For and While Loops with Collections"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "j2P7YI0orAPw"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Today, we will revisit **Python loops**, essential tools that simplify repetitive tasks. We will venture into the Python looping universe and acquire hands-on experience by applying loops to collections like `lists` and `strings`."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3zqjlqRctLko"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Understanding Looping"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "akqqElLLtiqu"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Have you ever experienced repeating a favorite song on a loop? That's what loops are all about in programming, too. For example, you can print greetings for a list of friends using a `for loop`:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "bMLg2wTOts0m"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "friends = ['Alice', 'Bob', 'Charlie', 'Daniel']\n",
        "# `friend` is the loop variable, taking each name in the `friends` list\n",
        "for friend in friends:\n",
        "    # for each `friend`, this line is executed\n",
        "    print(f'Hi {friend}, nice to meet you.')"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "WhXxbp68uJUn",
        "outputId": "f5dc55ae-5f79-414d-afe6-5c40d6042180"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Hi Alice, nice to meet you.\n",
            "Hi Bob, nice to meet you.\n",
            "Hi Charlie, nice to meet you.\n",
            "Hi Daniel, nice to meet you.\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Loops allow us to automate repetitive sequences efficiently."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "htuULz_lutp5"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## For Loop in Python"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7OTeAvkRuzm1"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In Python, a `for` loop works with any sequence, like `lists` or `strings`. Let's print a range of numbers using a `for` loop:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "_pLVI8pAvCjV"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# `num` runs through each number in the range of 5\n",
        "for num in range(5):\n",
        "    # This line will print numbers from 0 to 4\n",
        "    print(num)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "h1xXjMDjvZQM",
        "outputId": "1ff90d90-4264-47c3-85c1-a9b74ff5963b"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "0\n",
            "1\n",
            "2\n",
            "3\n",
            "4\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Each loop iteration updates the variable (`num`) to the next sequence value before executing the code block."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "GOHzAOCSvmlK"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## While Loop in Python"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "o_--Rsukvupx"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`While loops` execute code continuously until a condition becomes false. Here's a simple example:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "iV1VW6h8v6Kj"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "num = 0\n",
        "# The loop keeps running until num is greater than or equal to 5 i.e. num < 5\n",
        "while num < 5:\n",
        "    print(num)\n",
        "    # increase num by 1 each iteration\n",
        "    num += 1"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "xsJsZVmtwC3X",
        "outputId": "7c9aa12a-628c-4f64-ded0-b0d38d6cf779"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "0\n",
            "1\n",
            "2\n",
            "3\n",
            "4\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "As you can see, before each iteration, Python checks the condition (`num < 5`). If it's true, the code block runs; otherwise, Python exits the loop."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Ea8E3TquwYi_"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Looping Over Collections"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "_IzuVZqhykmN"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Python loops can directly work with collections, making it easy to handle elements of a `list` or `string`.\n",
        "\n",
        "For instance, consider looping over a list:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "EQL5ftAH4Mjf"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# list of fruits\n",
        "fruits = ['apple', 'banana', 'cherry']\n",
        "# `fruit` stands for each fruit in the `fruits` list\n",
        "for fruit in fruits:\n",
        "    print(fruit)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "Nbxguujq4XNZ",
        "outputId": "da4f676d-0adf-4a7c-84b7-33d11dd369b1"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "apple\n",
            "banana\n",
            "cherry\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "And, looping over a string:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hpfYTQUE49z6"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "word = 'hello'\n",
        "# `letter` is each individual character in the `word`\n",
        "for letter in word:\n",
        "    print(letter)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "5bbS749G5Bcv",
        "outputId": "667ddd74-f5e3-45a3-e37a-8175d6036bfe"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "h\n",
            "e\n",
            "l\n",
            "l\n",
            "o\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Applications of Looping"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "KxoP0Ddv5L3n"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Loops are integral to programming. They are used in various programming applications, such as summing numbers in a list or parsing text."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "yuN-VIlw5XxX"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# List of numbers\n",
        "numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n",
        "total = 0\n",
        "# `num` is each number in `numbers`\n",
        "for num in numbers:\n",
        "    total += num  # Add each number in the list\n",
        "print(total)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "CPSXNVWy5c-t",
        "outputId": "f0c30f36-c609-453e-d8db-14f426ddce1d"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "15\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# String\n",
        "text = 'hello'\n",
        "vowel_count = 0\n",
        "# `letter` is each character in `text`\n",
        "for letter in text:\n",
        "    # If a vowel letter is found, increment the count\n",
        "    if letter in 'aeiou':\n",
        "        vowel_count += 1\n",
        "print(vowel_count)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "b9wOB5GN5-d7",
        "outputId": "9b4c2300-26a3-426a-8e94-73a2ce11b5c3"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "2\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Lesson Summary"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "QxmyJCUt6im1"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Well done on getting a grasp of Python loops! We brushed up on looping fundamentals, Python's `for` and `while` loops, and how to loop over collections."
