      "source": [
        "Let's now explore character operations. Python provides various built-in functions, such as `ord()`, `chr()`, `upper()`, `lower()`, and `isalpha()`. We'll consider how such functions can prove advantageous in real-world scenarios, like data cleaning, where one might need to standardize the case of the text data.\n",
