    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Mastering Python String Methods and Type Conversions"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8v0edCTYCdMK"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In today's lesson, we'll explore Python's string methods: `split()`, `join()`, `strip()`, and learn how to perform type conversions. Python's robust built-in string methods simplify text processing, enhancing the readability and efficiency of our code."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2jhlUdg-Cmg8"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Understanding Python's 'split()' Function"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "aTgpL5PSCwQz"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Constructing strings frequently entails dividing them into smaller sections or 'tokens'. The `split()` function in Python achieves this goal by breaking a string into a list of substrings using a specified delimiter. If no delimiter is provided, it splits the string by a single whitespace character."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "sRF0Oy9pC8xF"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "sentence = 'Python is fun!'\n",
        "words = sentence.split()  # no delimiter provided, splitting by whitespace\n",
        "print(words)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "Hz3Kice0DcYg",
        "outputId": "ac831757-051c-4a3b-fcac-fa2ccdd2c8b7"
      },
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "['Python', 'is', 'fun!']\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In the example above, we observe that `split()` divides `sentence` into words. We can also opt for different delimiters, such as a comma."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6ba_Wan1DqVh"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "data = 'John,Doe,35,Engineer'\n",
        "info = data.split(',')  # provided a ',' delimiter\n",
        "print(info)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "LyqqMDiqDvrr",
        "outputId": "5894973e-15e8-466b-c1bf-70fc17026b0c"
      },
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "['John', 'Doe', '35', 'Engineer']\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exploring the 'join()' Method"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "jmZ399mzD-Fh"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Conversely, Python's `join()` method concatenates, or 'joins', strings into a single string:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1IzQBBtEEBX2"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "words = ['Programming', 'with', 'Python', 'is', 'exciting!']\n",
        "sentence = ' '.join(words)\n",
        "print(sentence)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "GiK806xdEGLo",
        "outputId": "d6c92173-4bb3-44c5-8b8a-910593e13480"
      },
      "execution_count": 4,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Programming with Python is exciting!\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Here, `join()` takes a list of words, which are strings, and merges them into a sentence — a single string, using a space as a delimiter."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SftcXaxyEVee"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Mastering the 'strip()' Method"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BQdfC73gEY_W"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Discerning extra spaces in strings can prove challenging, and they may lead to problems. Python's `strip()` method removes leading and trailing spaces, tab or newline characters from a string:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "lxPPgfEjEjh3"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "name = '    John Doe    \\t\\n'\n",
        "name = name.strip()\n",
        "print(name)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "kDC5pCTwEnp3",
        "outputId": "e3d06c12-60c7-4c11-8aa7-8ecb416f731b"
      },
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "John Doe\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Furthermore, we can use `lstrip()` and `rstrip()` to remove spaces, tabs, and newline characters from the left and right of a string, respectively:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6gFN0tv1E09l"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "name = '    John Doe    '\n",
        "print(name.lstrip())\n",
        "print(name.rstrip())"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "z2cer3TxE5VO",
        "outputId": "78df8812-7e12-4279-dd05-8ca776a851d6"
      },
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "John Doe    \n",
            "    John Doe\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Python Type Conversions"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "I0E1p-GcFDzn"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Python's built-in type conversion functions, such as `int()`, `str()`, `float()`, and `bool()`, enable the switching between different data types:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0xzIYDwZFIrY"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "num_str = '123'\n",
        "print(type(num_str))\n",
        "num = int(num_str)\n",
        "print(type(num))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "VJMGkgZDFSND",
        "outputId": "f5e39e83-4be1-4337-baac-4ef9007f84eb"
      },
      "execution_count": 7,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "<class 'str'>\n",
            "<class 'int'>\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We can also employ `str()` to convert a number to a string, which proves handy for concatenating a string with a number:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "UM0bAApLGD8V"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "name = 'John'\n",
        "age = 25\n",
        "print('My name is ' + name + ', and I am ' + str(age) + ' years old.')"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "UbBRl4c6GKds",
        "outputId": "ed538c1b-c81d-4d59-ad90-a05949b4f1b4"
      },
      "execution_count": 8,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "My name is John, and I am 25 years old.\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Combining split(), join(), strip(), and Type Conversions Together"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "xYhwwXICGhDF"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In specific scenarios, we need to combine all these methods. One such scenario could be the task of calculating the average of a string of numbers separated by commas:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "eqeRROaIGmh9"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "numbers = '1,2,3,4,5'\n",
        "# Convert string to a list of numbers\n",
        "num_list = [int(num) for num in numbers.split(',')]\n",
        "print(num_list)\n",
        "# Calculate average\n",
        "average = sum(num_list) / len(num_list)\n",
        "print(f'Average: {average}')"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "KBIPYfpdGtWd",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "e74c781c-082c-4728-9f69-39918488fa0e"
      },
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\n",
            "Average: 3.0\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "By integrating these methods, we can transform the string `'1,2,3,4,5'` into a list of numbers, calculate their average, and display the result."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "H6AwrlUoHO86"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
